; portraits.eval - a member's portrait is an id that round-trips through a save.
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -headless -eval <path to this file>, then read dungeon.log.
; What it should show (docs/portraits-plan.md, phase 2):
;   - the four defaults, each loaded (no "NOT LOADED");
;   - Sera changed to corax001;
;   - a reset puts Sera back on her default;
;   - loading the save brings corax001 back.
; (An id the catalog lacks is refused - `portrait 3 no_such_portrait` - but a
; refusal fails the run, so that is checked by hand, not here.)

logecho on
reset
portrait

portrait 1 corax001
save eval_portraits

reset
portrait 1

load eval_portraits
portrait
